WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:22.893
After the frightening episode in the Gorbeau house, Marius moved into his friend Courfeyrac's apartment.

2
00:00:22.894 --> 00:00:29.067
Marius tried to work, but he was too distracted with worry. What had become of the Lark?

3
00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:34.789
Every day he went to a park called The Field of the Lark and sat there thinking of her.

4
00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:44.535
One day in April, he heard a familiar voice call his name. Marius looked up and recognized the elder Thenardier girl, Eponine.

5
00:00:44.536 --> 00:00:51.747
She was still clothed in rags, but now she had straw in her hair, probably from sleeping in a stable.

6
00:00:51.748 --> 00:00:56.106
Despite this, she looked almost beautiful.

7
00:00:56.107 --> 00:01:05.274
"I spent two weeks in jail, and when I got out, you'd moved," said Eponine. "I've spent the last six weeks looking for you."

8
00:01:05.275 --> 00:01:11.433
Marius said nothing. He didn't want to have anything to do with this girl or her family.

9
00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:17.179
"I have the address you wanted me to get," said Eponine.

10
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.477
Marius turned pale. "What address?"

11
00:01:20.478 --> 00:01:22.353
"For the young lady."

12
00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:27.345
Marius sprang from his seat and grabbed her hands. "Take me there at once!"

13
00:01:27.346 --> 00:01:34.512
"Oh, how happy you are!" A cloud crossed Eponine's face as she pulled away her hands.

14
00:01:34.513 --> 00:01:40.178
"Promise me, Eponine, that you won't tell your father—or anyone—where she is."

15
00:01:40.179 --> 00:01:44.757
"It's lovely to hear you say my name," Eponine said dreamily.

16
00:01:44.758 --> 00:01:46.077
"Promise me!"

17
00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:49.908
"All right, I promise. Now follow me."

18
00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:55.083
On the Rue Plumet, there stood a two-story house in a large garden.

19
00:01:55.084 --> 00:02:03.575
Behind this house was a smaller building and a gate leading onto another street. This is where Eponine led Marius.

20
00:02:03.576 --> 00:02:11.043
Several years earlier Jean Valjean had come to live there with Cosette and a female servant named Toussaint.

21
00:02:11.044 --> 00:02:17.146
While Cosette and Toussaint stayed in the main house, he slept in the smaller one.

22
00:02:17.147 --> 00:02:22.567
The neighbors didn't gossip about these new residents because there were no neighbors.

23
00:02:22.568 --> 00:02:27.289
Valjean rented the house using the name Ultimus Fauchelevent.

24
00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:36.535
Before then, Valjean and Cosette had been living happily at the convent. But as time passed Valjean began to feel guilty.

25
00:02:36.536 --> 00:02:40.638
If they stayed, he knew that Cosette would become a nun.

26
00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:46.122
It wouldn't be fair to make her retreat from life without first experiencing it.

27
00:02:46.123 --> 00:02:50.852
He also didn't want her to blame him if she ever regretted becoming a nun.

28
00:02:50.853 --> 00:02:58.939
Five years had passed since their arrival at the convent, and few people in the outside world would recognize him now.

29
00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:06.590
Besides, Cosette had almost completed her education, so Valjean decided it was time to move out.

30
00:03:06.591 --> 00:03:12.844
He paid the nuns for Cosette's education, and then the two of them left the convent.

31
00:03:12.845 --> 00:03:17.947
In addition to the Rue Plumet house, he had rented two other apartments.

32
00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:24.237
One was on the Rue de l'Ouest and the other on the Rue de l'Homme Armé.

33
00:03:24.238 --> 00:03:32.753
Never again would he be trapped as he'd been at the Gorbeau house. Every month or so, they moved from one house to another.

34
00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:40.325
Wherever they moved, he took the small suitcase containing the mourning outfit he had brought to the Thenardiers' inn.

35
00:03:40.326 --> 00:03:45.912
Cosette didn't know what was inside the suitcase, but she liked to tease him about it.

36
00:03:45.913 --> 00:03:50.230
"You're inseparable from that thing. I'm quite jealous!"

37
00:03:50.231 --> 00:03:54.863
As the years passed, Cosette began to grow more beautiful.

38
00:03:54.864 --> 00:03:59.642
She abandoned her convent school uniform for more fashionable clothing.

39
00:03:59.643 --> 00:04:08.626
Her growing beauty caused Valjean a deep anguish. Men would notice her. It was likely that someday she would leave him.

40
00:04:08.627 --> 00:04:16.705
It was about this time that Marius noticed Cosette's beauty. She also noticed Marius and fell in love with him.

41
00:04:16.706 --> 00:04:22.626
Observing this, Valjean stopped taking her to the Luxembourg Gardens.

42
00:04:22.627 --> 00:04:28.611
Cosette did not protest because she didn't want Valjean to know that she was interested in Marius.

43
00:04:28.612 --> 00:04:33.682
Instead she simply looked sad, which made Valjean sad.

44
00:04:33.683 --> 00:04:41.523
Cosette continued to sit with her father every evening and to accompany him when he brought food and clothing to the poor.

45
00:04:41.524 --> 00:04:47.844
The day after their visit to the Thenardiers, Valjean arrived home with a large burn on his arm.

46
00:04:47.845 --> 00:04:50.507
It took more than a month to heal.

47
00:04:50.508 --> 00:04:54.795
At the beginning of April, Valjean went away for a few days.

48
00:04:54.796 --> 00:04:58.666
He often did this when they needed money to run the household.

49
00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:05.086
One evening Cosette was sitting alone in the parlor when she heard footsteps in the garden.

50
00:05:05.087 --> 00:05:14.165
She ran up to her room and looked outside, but no one was there. Cosette thought no more about it; she was not easily startled.

51
00:05:14.166 --> 00:05:19.237
The next evening she was walking in the garden when she thought she saw a shadow.

52
00:05:19.238 --> 00:05:26.570
It looked like a man wearing a hat. For a moment she could not speak or turn her head.

53
00:05:26.571 --> 00:05:31.657
But then she gathered her courage and turned around. No one was there.

54
00:05:31.658 --> 00:05:38.467
Cosette looked behind bushes and in the dark corners of the garden. Still she found no one.

55
00:05:38.468 --> 00:05:43.249
When Valjean returned the next day, Cosette told him what had happened.

56
00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:48.221
She expected him to say, "Oh, you were just being a foolish girl."

57
00:05:48.222 --> 00:05:55.610
Instead he looked anxious and announced that he would search the garden. That night he summoned her outside.

58
00:05:55.611 --> 00:06:02.189
"Look, I've found your man with the hat." Valjean pointed to a chimney making a shadow on the grass.

59
00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:10.927
Cosette smiled. "I was just being foolish," she said. But this shadow didn't disappear when she turned around to look at it.

60
00:06:10.928 --> 00:06:16.768
A few nights later, Valjean was out, and Cosette was sitting on a bench in the garden.

61
00:06:16.769 --> 00:06:24.181
She decided to stroll among the plants. When she returned to her bench, there was a stone on it.

62
00:06:24.182 --> 00:06:29.268
"That wasn't there before," she said to herself. "Who put it there?"

63
00:06:29.269 --> 00:06:34.832
She ran into the house and told Toussaint to lock all the doors and windows.

64
00:06:34.833 --> 00:06:42.261
The next morning Cosette felt rather silly. "There was no stone on that bench, just as there was no man with a hat!"

65
00:06:42.262 --> 00:06:49.586
She went boldly into the garden and marched right up to the bench. The stone was holding down a letter on the bench.

66
00:06:49.587 --> 00:06:54.999
The envelope did not have a name on it, but Cosette assumed it was meant for her.

67
00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:00.070
She opened it and found four pieces of paper covered with writing.

68
00:07:00.071 --> 00:07:08.158
There was no signature at the end. Cosette began to read and immediately realized this was a love letter.

69
00:07:08.159 --> 00:07:15.888
Who could have written it? Cosette had no doubts. It was from the handsome young man in the Luxembourg Gardens.

70
00:07:15.889 --> 00:07:20.896
She carried the letter up to her room and spent the day rereading it.

71
00:07:20.897 --> 00:07:23.634
That night she went out into the garden.

72
00:07:23.635 --> 00:07:29.467
Marius stepped onto the path in front of her. "Forgive me if I've frightened you.

73
00:07:29.468 --> 00:07:34.880
My heart is bursting with love, and I couldn't remain hidden one moment longer."

74
00:07:34.881 --> 00:07:42.880
Marius explained how he had lurked in the garden and watched her the past few nights. Cosette took his hand.

75
00:07:42.881 --> 00:07:46.967
"Does this mean that you love me too?" asked Marius.

76
00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:54.785
She nodded and then they kissed. They talked for hours, describing how they had adored each other from afar.

77
00:07:54.786 --> 00:08:04.353
When they had told each other almost everything, Cosette laid her head on his shoulder and said, "My name is Cosette. What's yours?"

78
00:08:04.354 --> 00:08:05.706
"Marius."

79
00:08:05.707 --> 00:08:12.925
Cosette never asked Marius how he got into the garden. It seemed so natural that he was there.
